  "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 15-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 15-layer planar multilayer stack on Al substrate with material sequence Cr/HfO2/SiO2/Cr/HfO2/SiO2/Cr/HfO2/SiO2/Cr/HfO2/SiO2/Cr/HfO2. Initialize thicknesses with asymmetric perturbation: SiO2 layers at positions 2,4,6,8,12 set to quarter-wave optical thickness minus 10 nm, HfO2 layers at positions 1,3,5,7,11,13 set to quarter-wave optical thickness plus 10 nm, central layers 5-9 locked at baseline QWOT values. Apply thickness bounds 30-300 nm for all finite layers. Optimize at normal incidence for unpolarized light. Target: maximize mean absorptance in 400-700 nm band and maximize mean reflectance in 700-2000 nm band. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with reduced step-size to avoid physics violations observed in prior iterations. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
